//! Canonical ABI scratch migration anchor (`std::component`, #044, #917).
//!
//! The former `canonical_lower_string` / `canonical_lift_string` /
//! `canonical_lift_string_at` / `canonical_lower_list_i32` /
//! `canonical_lift_list_i32` / `canonical_lift_list_i32_at` /
//! `canonical_scratch_new` free functions were retired by the #917 component
//! wave (ADR-044/ADR-046). Callers migrate to the associated functions on
//! `Component` from `use std::component::Component`; `CanonicalSlice` now
//! lives in `std::component` as well.
//!
//! The module itself stays until the 1.0.0 era so qualified calls resolve to
//! an E0100 migration hint instead of an undefined-module error; delete it
//! once the removal window closes.
